# Trivy ignore file for vulnerabilities with no upstream fix.
# Each entry is a CVE or GHSA ID, one per line.

# =============================================================================
# ecdsa: Minerva timing attack on P-256 (CVE-2024-23342 / GHSA-wj6h-64fc-37mp)
# Alert #678 — The ecdsa project considers side-channel attacks "out of scope"
# and there is no planned fix for any version. The application mitigates this by
# using python-jose[cryptography], which routes EC operations through the
# cryptography/OpenSSL backend instead of the vulnerable pure-Python ecdsa
# implementation. The app also restricts jwt.decode to a single algorithm
# (HS256) in app/core/security.py, preventing algorithm-confusion exploitation.
CVE-2024-23342
